Dear GLD & Administrative Court,

=20

I hope this message finds you well. Unfortunately, this order is the first =
notification we have received in relation to the Judicial review. We have no=
t been served with the application or grounds for the Judicial review and, t=
herefore, without the provision of these documents, we are unable to acknowl=
edge service on behalf of HMCTS.

=20

Could you please provide us with the necessary documents at your earliest c=
onvenience? This would enable us to proceed accordingly and fulfil our oblig=
ations.

=20

Thank you for your prompt attention to this matter.

=20

Kind regards,

=20

T. Kemp | User Investigations Officer (Litigation)

User Investigations Team | Service Excellence & Delivery Division |

HM Courts & Tribunals Service

Email: Litigationteam.HMCTS@justice.gov.uk=20

=20

=20

=20

Here is how HMCTS uses personal data about you

=20

=20

From: Administrative Court Office, Paper Results <administrativecourtoffice=
.paperresults@justice.gov.uk>=20
Sent: 04 December 2025 12:00
To: 'Nadia@rosekross.com' <Nadia@rosekross.com>
Cc: New Proceedings <newproceedings@governmentlegal.gov.uk>; TheTreasurySol=
