LitigationTeam.HMCTS@justice.gov.uk>
Subject: AC-2025-LON-004293 Zahmoul) v Secretary of State for Justice and P=
ermanent Secretary

=20

Dear Sir/Madam,=20

=20

Please find attached order by the Hon. Mrs Justice Lieven by way of service=
.=20

=20

Kind regards,=20

=20

Hilary Sober| Paper Results Team | King=E2=80=99s Bench Division | HMCTS | Royal =
Courts of Justice| Strand, London | WC2A 2LL | Phone: 020 7947 6000 | Web: w=
ww.gov.uk/hmcts

=20

Listing Enquiries: administrativecourtoffice.listoffice@justice.gov.uk

General Enquiries:  administrativecourtoffice.generaloffice@justice.gov.uk

Civil Enquiries: administrativecourtoffice.caseprogression@justice.gov.uk

Criminal & Extradition Enquiries: administrativecourtoffice.crimex@justice.=
gov.uk

=20

For information on how HMCTS uses personal data about you please see: https=
://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/hm-courts-and-tribunals-service/about=
/personal-information-charter

=20

=20

=20
This e-mail and any attachments is intended only for the attention of the a=
ddressee(s). Its unauthorised use, disclosure, storage or copying is not per=
mitted. If you are not the intended recipient, please destroy all copies and=
 inform the sender by return e-mail. Internet e-mail is not a secure medium.=
 Any reply to this message could be intercepted and read by someone else. Pl=
ease bear that in mind when deciding whether to send material in response to=
 this message by e-mail. This e-mail (whether you are the sender or the reci=
pient) may be monitored, recorded and retained by the Ministry of Justice. M=
onitoring / blocking software may be used, and e-mail content may be read at=
 any time. You have a responsibility to ensure laws are not broken when comp=
osing or forwarding e-mails and their contents. 

